    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Slosh',
            subtitle: 'Domino Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Slosh is a four-handed British domino game from the Trains family, played with a double-six set. The engine tile is placed in the center; each player has a train (a line of tiles) extending from the engine toward them. On your turn you add a tile to your own train if you can; if you cannot, the next player may slosh (play on your train) then play on their own. The round ends when someone dominoes or the game is blocked; lowest pip count in hand wins the round. Scoring is with poker chips or pencil.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'British member of the Trains family. The name refers to water or liquid spilling over (sloshing), evoking splashing someone at a bar.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Four players. A four-handed British domino game; each player has their own train extending from the center engine toward them, and play proceeds to the left.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Double-six domino set. Each player receives six tiles; four tiles form the boneyard and are not used in the round.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Double-six domino set, markers or poker chips (or pencil) for scoring.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Each player gets six tiles. The engine for the first round is the double-four; if it is in the boneyard, the hand is redealt until someone has it. The player with the engine places it first; play proceeds to the left.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
