          deckDescription: 'A double-six domino set comprising 28 tiles. Each tile has two ends with zero to six pips (spots). Every combination from 0-0 (blank) through 6-6 appears exactly once. The set is used for connecting and train games.',
          suitDescription: 'Dominoes use pip values zero through six on each end; matching is by end value. There are no traditional suits; connectivity is determined by the pip count on the open end of each train.',
          rankDescription: 'Each half of a tile has a rank from zero (blank) to six pips. Tiles are matched by placing a tile with an end that matches the open end of the train.',
